501
00:32:19,460 --> 00:32:28,980
While Con Ed boils water to provide steam heat, the goal of other companies, like the California Bottling Company, is to turn steam back into water.

502
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:34,880
The facility processes and packages a variety of water products, including distilled water.

503
00:32:36,440 --> 00:32:40,320
Distillation involves boiling water and vaporizing it into steam.

504
00:32:40,321 --> 00:32:46,700
Boiling sterilizes the water, and when the steam lifts out of it, salts and other solids

505
00:32:46,701 --> 00:32:48,560
are left behind.

506
00:32:48,561 --> 00:32:53,200
Then the steam is cooled, and when it condenses back into liquid form, it's as close to pure

507
00:32:53,201 --> 00:32:57,380
H2O as possible.

508
00:32:57,381 --> 00:33:02,260
While distillation can produce clean water from a very contaminated source, California

509
00:33:02,261 --> 00:33:05,180
bottling begins with the municipal water supply.

510
00:33:05,181 --> 00:33:11,180
It arrives in the pipe above, fairly directly from the Sierras, as it turns out.

511
00:33:11,181 --> 00:33:14,180
But we treat it before processing through the distiller.

512
00:33:14,181 --> 00:33:18,180
First, we run it through some sand filters to take out particulate matter.

513
00:33:18,181 --> 00:33:22,180
We run it through carbon filters to take out chlorine that might be present.

514
00:33:22,181 --> 00:33:26,180
And then we run it through softeners to take out the hardness.

515
00:33:26,181 --> 00:33:31,180
All this is done to provide a very clean water before we even enter the distillation process.

516
00:33:31,181 --> 00:33:34,180
The facility has several stills.

517
00:33:34,181 --> 00:33:38,640
The largest output approximately 1,000 gallons of distilled water per hour.

518
00:33:39,840 --> 00:33:42,620
To eliminate any contaminants picked up in the system,

519
00:33:43,140 --> 00:33:45,660
the distilled water runs through submicron filters

520
00:33:45,661 --> 00:33:49,560
and then into a tank where ozone gas bubbles up through it

521
00:33:49,561 --> 00:33:51,380
to treat any remaining impurities.

522
00:33:53,080 --> 00:33:54,700
Now it's ready for bottling.

523
00:33:55,260 --> 00:33:58,060
This is about as per as you can get for water.

524
00:33:58,220 --> 00:34:00,840
It's half a part or so per million of dissolved solids.

525
00:34:00,841 --> 00:34:07,060
The water in the gallon containers is an all-purpose product that's recommended for use in steam irons.

526
00:34:07,660 --> 00:34:11,220
But compared to regular water, distilled water is relatively tasteless.

527
00:34:12,420 --> 00:34:16,060
So when the California Bottling Company makes specialty-label drinking waters,

528
00:34:16,560 --> 00:34:21,000
these tanks are brought online to add back brand-specific electrolytes and minerals.

529
00:34:21,680 --> 00:34:26,160
These actually make the water healthier to drink and give it a more appealing taste.

